                <pb facs="0541" n="443" xml:id="pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3390: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-14T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1920—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:17 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>184. The President has issued a conventional mandate ordering troops of
                    contending sides to return to their original posts, thus saving the people from
                    miseries of war. Will probably be entirely disregarded. Joint telegram opposing
                    Tuan received from the eight military governors whose union seems complete.
                    Martial law is proclaimed in Peking by Tuan officials acting without President’s
                    approbation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
